[{"id":126024,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126024\">#49</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Separate the discussion of Orton and Pitts’s decomposition of univalence from discussion of weaker variants of univalence.</li>\n<li>An attempt (could be improved) to group the references into sections.</li>\n<li>Clean up some notation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I hope to do some more work on this page in the future.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/115\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/115\">v115</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789029961,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126025,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126025\">#50</a> I would suggest deleting the section on \"Internal univalence\", which is observing in a rather long-winded way that if a universe $U$ is closed under <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/identity+types\">identity types</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dependent+product+types\">dependent product types</a>, and <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types\">dependent sum types</a>, then for $A, B : U$ the type $A \\simeq B$ can be encoded as an element of $U$.</p>","timestamp":1789031767,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126026,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126026\">#51</a> Thanks for catching and flagging. </p>\n<p>This section, “Internal univalence”, was added in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/78\">revision 78</a> by the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Anonymous+User#InThePast\">infamous Anonymous user</a> (part of an edit spree to this entry by them throughout winter 2022/23).</p>\n<p>So I am not surprised to hear that it’s low quality. Please go ahead and delete it!</p>","timestamp":1789035954,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126027,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126027\">#52</a> Remove the “internal univalence” section as proposed.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/116\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/116\">v116</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789036336,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126031,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126031\">#53</a> Clarify and update canonicity section</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/118\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/118\">v118</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789155875,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126032,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126032\">#54</a> Clean up the introduction. Add a reference for inconsistency of the global choice operator with univalence</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/121\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/121\">v121</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789224420,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126036,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126036\">#55</a> Generalize section on Axiom K to discuss h-levels of univalent universes</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/122\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/122\">v122</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789317507,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126056,"sender_id":612,"sender_full_name":"nLab edit announcer","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c58b62e30f75d369349d5c08eee8f6b9?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126056\">#56</a> added a section on the relation between univalence and large elimination of the interval type</p>\n<p>zulip chat viewer</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/124\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/124\">v124</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789872026,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126252,"sender_id":1347,"sender_full_name":"Evan Cavallo","avatar_url":"/user_avatars/2/a3b7e6a8707328c9cf37228057769cad21b6e7fb.png","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/univalence.20axiom/near/126252\">#57</a> Mention the cardinal model</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/univalence+axiom/125\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/univalence+axiom/125\">v125</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/univalence+axiom\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1792498861,"subject":"univalence axiom","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]